                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 38-year-old male, admitted on 18/09/2011 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. Physical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with guarding. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis without evidence of perforation. The patient underwent laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on 19/09/2011 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, intravenous antibiotics and analgesics were administered, and recovery was uneventful. Wound care was performed prior to discharge on 20/09/2011. The patient was advised on wound hygiene and signs of complications. Please arrange follow-up in approximately two weeks. Should any concerns arise, do not hesitate to contact us. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
